[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Start "flank-exchange 2...d5"]
[Name "3.e3: the quiet English"]

3. e3 { Solid, but it shuts in the c1 bishop. }
3... Nf6 { Develops and waits. Black's moves do not change. }
4. cxd5 { White swaps now. 4.d4 goes straight into a Queen's Gambit Declined, where ...Be7 is the move again. }
4... exd5 { Taking back with the knight scores worse: White gets 52% against it and 47% against the pawn, and the engine prefers the pawn. }
5. d4
5... Be7 { The plan is the same as everywhere else. The engine likes ...Bd6 or ...c6 slightly more, but the position is level either way. }
6. Nf3
6... O-O
7. Bd3
7... c6 { Holds d5 for good. Black's next moves are ...Nbd7, ...Re8 and ...Nf8, as in the Exchange Variation, and the c1 bishop is still shut in behind e3. White scores 48%. [%csl Gd5] } *
